  "configuration_id": "config_021",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_011 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + transformer + concat, multimodal/multiprofile) achieved 0.688 accuracy at 5.16 GPU hours, establishing a baseline for the multimodal multiprofile pipeline. The most uncertain and high-impact design choice remaining is the image encoder: ResNet50 is a relatively modest feature extractor compared to ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L, which typically provides substantially richer visual representations. Question: Does upgrading the image encoder from ResNet50 to imagenet_vit_l (while holding all other hyperparameters identical) meaningfully improve validation accuracy? This is a clean single-variable A/B test against config_011, so any accuracy delta can be attributed to the image encoder. Rationale: With 8 experiments remaining, investing in the most likely source of a meaningful accuracy gain now is the best use of the next slot. A stronger image encoder is the highest-leverage architectural upgrade available. Expected relative cost: ViT-L has ~2-3× the parameters of ResNet50, so I estimate ~7-9 GPU hours (roughly 1.5× the cost of config_011). This is a justified premium given the potential accuracy lift, and the total budget still leaves room for 7 further experiments."
}

